# NOTE FOR ANYONE ADDING ZENODO METADATA LATER.
# Zenodo reads this file when archiving a GitHub release, BUT if a .zenodo.json is also present it
# uses that and ignores this file silently. Do not add a .zenodo.json alongside this one unless you
# intend it to be the single source of truth, or a minted DOI will carry whichever metadata is
# stale. This repository deliberately keeps CITATION.cff only.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "An Agent That Copies Nobody Is Certified as a Leader"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jacob
    given-names: Manu Nicholas
    email: manunicholasjacob@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
abstract: >-
  An audit of information-theoretic influence detection on real multi-agent chat. The conventional
  circular-shift surrogate is invalid on turn-ordered agent logs (family-wise error rate 0.90 against
  a nominal 0.05); a symbol-permutation surrogate restores it to 0.063, and a conditional estimate
  additionally removes common-cause edges. Also reports a symbolisation floor: below an adjusted
  Rand index of about 0.44 between symboliser and truth, detection collapses regardless of estimator.
keywords:
  - transfer entropy
  - multi-agent systems
  - AI safety
  - surrogate data
  - coordination detection
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
